; a map with a SINGLE keyless entry (`{ bytes }`). Like `map_entry_no_key` (`{ bytes, uint }`) this
; is rejected by design ("map fields need keys"), but it exercises a DIFFERENT parse path: the
; 1-entry branch of `parse_group_type`, which used to `panic!("unsupported table map key (2)")` on a
; single `TypeGroupname` map entry. It now falls through to the Heterogenous path and funnels into
; `parse_record_from_group_choice`'s graceful rejection. Pins that the single-entry form stays
; `error (graceful)`; a regression re-introducing the panic flips this back to PANIC.
m = { bytes }
